{"id": "herm-Q27979350", "status": "ok", "meta": "Napoleon inspects the Imperial Guard at the Tuileries while a wounded veteran hands him a petition, painted by Horace Vernet in 1838.", "about": "Napoleon inspects a parade of the Imperial Guard in the Place du Carrousel outside the Tuileries Palace around 1808, and a wounded veteran holds out a petition to him. The officers with him include Eugène de Beauharnais, Joachim Murat, Michel Ney, Jean-Andoche Junot and Géraud Duroc. The Horses of Saint Mark, taken from Venice and returned in 1815, can be seen at the right. Horace Vernet painted it in 1838. Nicholas I bought it from him for the Hermitage, and a copy is in the Wallace Collection in London.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ANapol%C3%A9on_aux_Tuileries_-_Horace_Vernet.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ANapol%C3%A9on_aux_Tuileries_-_Horace_Vernet.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27979350", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon_at_the_Tuileries"], "check": "clean"}
