{"id": "cma-707624", "status": "ok", "meta": "A courtesan lights her pipe from a young samurai's at a cherry-blossom party on Gotenyama in Edo, a scroll by Utagawa Toyokuni.", "about": "A courtesan lights her pipe from the pipe of a fashionably dressed young man of samurai rank, at the center of a cherry-blossom party on Gotenyama, Palace Hill, in Edo. Five adults and a child stand at the top of the hill, and the smoke billows up to the sky. The museum adds that tobacco came to Japan with Portuguese traders around the 1550s. Utagawa Toyokuni made the hanging scroll in the late 1700s or early 1800s.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/2026.46", "inventory_number": "2026.46", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "The Kelvin Smith Collection, given by Ellen and Bruce Mavec", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/2026.46", "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/707624"], "check": "clean"}
