{"id": "cma-150841", "status": "ok", "meta": "A painter in an 18th-century costume works on a small canvas of a nymph and a satyr in Ernest Meissonier's A Painter, 1855.", "about": "A painter in an 18th-century costume works on a small canvas of a nymph and a satyr. Meissonier often showed artists and musicians of the 1600s and 1700s at work. The costume was nearly a hundred years out of date when he painted it, which makes the scene a historical fiction. To get details right he collected accessories from local costume markets for what he called a work library. He showed the painting at the Paris Salon of 1857.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1982.247", "inventory_number": "1982.247", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "Gift of Mrs. Noah L. Butkin", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/1982.247", "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/150841"], "check": "clean"}
