{"id": "aic-8900", "status": "ok", "meta": "A young woman lost in thought walks under a willow in a black kimono with phoenix obi, a scroll by Isoda Koryusai, about 1780.", "about": "A young woman strolls under a willow tree, lost in thought. She wears a black kimono over layers of red and an obi embroidered with phoenixes, elaborate dress that suggests she is on her way to some engagement. The museum says the rich patterns and colors of her clothes stand out against the sparse landscape painted in ink. Isoda Koryusai made the hanging scroll around 1780.", "museum_record": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/8900", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "100.2 × 32.6 cm (39 7/16 × 12 7/8 in.); Overall with mount and knobs: 184 × 52.4 cm (72 7/16 × 20 5/8 in.)", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.artic.edu/artworks/8900"], "check": "clean"}
