{"id": "wd-Q15906986", "status": "ok", "meta": "Jacob tricks his blind father Isaac with a sheepskin on his arm in Jusepe de Ribera's painting of 1637 in the Prado.", "about": "Jacob, helped by his mother Rebekah, tricks his blind father Isaac into giving him the blessing meant for his brother Esau. He covers one arm with a sheepskin to imitate Esau's hairy arms, and Isaac lies on the bed feeling it. Jusepe de Ribera painted it in 1637, and Wikipedia says critics count it among his most mature works. Nobody knows who ordered it. It was in the Royal Alcázar in Madrid by 1734 and is now in the Prado.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibera_-_Isaac_y_Jacob%2C_P001118.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibera_-_Isaac_y_Jacob%2C_P001118.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15906986", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_and_Jacob"], "check": "clean"}
{"id": "met-435852", "status": "ok", "meta": "Two children tease a cat with a shrimp claw in Annibale Carracci's painting of about 1587 to 1588.", "about": "Two children play a cruel prank on a cat. The boy holds a shrimp and tries to put its claw into the cat's right ear, and the cat has already turned wary. Annibale Carracci painted it around 1587 to 1588, probably while he was staying in Venice, since the influence of Tintoretto and other Venetian painters shows. Roberto Longhi gave it to Annibale instead of Agostino. The Metropolitan Museum acquired it in 1994.", "museum_record": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/435852", "inventory_number": "1994.142", "dimensions": "26 x 35 in. (66 x 88.9 cm)", "credit_line": "Purchase, Gwynne Andrews Fund, and Bequests of Collis P. Huntington and Ogden Mills, by exchange, 1994", "sources": ["https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/435852", "https://collectionapi.metmuseum.org/public/collection/v1/objects/435852", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17629102", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Children_Teasing_a_Cat"], "check": "clean"}
