{"id": "si-chndm_1938-88-8673", "status": "ok", "meta": "Caius Marius in prison as two Cimbrian soldiers enter his cell, an engraving by Giorgio Ghisi, about 1560.", "about": "Caius Marius sits at the right with one hand clutching his chest and the other stretched toward two Cimbrian soldiers who enter his cell. A window at the center shows classical ruins, with light streaming through the clouds toward him. A small tablet at lower left carries a signature. Giorgio Ghisi made the print around 1560.", "museum_record": "https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/69764", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://collection.cooperhewitt.org/view/objects/asitem/id/69764"], "check": "clean"}
